 • Duration: ~8.5 minutes (started 2026-08-18 07:39:09 UTC, ended 07:47:39 UTC) 
 • Severity: Critical                                                           
 • Status: Active (alert was firing at investigation time 07:43:54 UTC)         

Root Cause: The postgres database deployment has no running, ready replicas.    
This means the database is completely unavailable, likely causing failures in   
any shop application components that depend on it.                              

Possible Causes:                                                                

 1 Pod crash loop - containers failing to start due to misconfiguration, missing
   dependencies, or application errors                                          
 2 Resource constraints - insufficient CPU/memory on nodes preventing pod       
   scheduling                                                                   
 3 Image pull failures - unable to pull the postgres container image            
 4 Node issues - nodes unavailable or pods evicted                              
 5 Configuration errors - invalid environment variables, missing                
   secrets/configmaps, or volume mount issues                                   

Investigation Blocked: Unable to complete deeper investigation due to Kubernetes
API connectivity issues (connection refused to 127.0.0.1:6444). The cluster API 
server appears unreachable from the investigation environment.                  

Recommended Actions:                                                            

 1 Check postgres deployment: kubectl get deployment postgres -n shop           
 2 Inspect pod status: kubectl get pods -n shop -l deployment=postgres          
 3 Review pod events: kubectl describe deployment postgres -n shop              
 4 Check logs: kubectl logs -n shop -l deployment=postgres --tail=100           
 5 Verify node capacity and pod resource requests                               
